<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Roboto:wght@400;700&display=swap');

        body {
            font-family: 'Roboto', Arial, sans-serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 40px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.4;
            background: #ffffff;
        }

        /* Simulate columns via flex */
        .columns {
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        .column {
            flex: 1;
        }

        /* Header */
        h1 {
            font-size: 28px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        /* Paragraphs */
        p {
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        /* Bullet list */
        ul {
            padding-left: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        /* Placeholder for diagram/chart */
        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 220px;
            background: #f0f0f0;
            margin: 25px 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            border: 1px dashed #999;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #555;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .placeholder-caption {
            font-size: 14px;
            margin-top: 8px;
            color: #666;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Sample Document Layout</h1>

    <p>This is a sample multi-column document for demonstration of spatial layout conversion.</p>

    <div class="columns">
        <!-- Left column -->
        <div class="column">
            <p>Paragraph one in column one. This text appears on the left side of the page with typical newspaper-style justification.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>First bullet point</li>
                <li>Second bullet point</li>
                <li>Third bullet point</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Right column -->
        <div class="column">
            <p>Paragraph two in column two. This text is placed directly beside the first column using CSS flexbox to replicate side-by-side alignment.</p>
            <p>Additional text continues here to show how the layout would flow if there were more lines.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="placeholder">
        [Chart: centered at bottom of page]
    </div>
    <div class="placeholder-caption">[Diagram: top-right]</div>

    <p>Footer text that would appear at the very bottom of the document.</p>
</body>
</html>
```
